    "summary": "Fire‑filled NYE set with killer Mason's Children and long Dancin' In The Street",
    "blurb": "The Boston Tea Party show delivers a gritty Jerry Garcia guitar tone, Tom Constanten’s thick keyboard runs, and standout performances of Mason's Children, Easy Wind and Black Peter. A monster 15‑minute Dancin' In The Street caps the second set, while the band’s New Year’s Eve banter adds priceless atmosphere.",
    "review": "On December 29, 1969 the Grateful Dead wrapped up the year at Boston’s Tea Party with a set that still feels fresh and fierce. Jerry’s guitar is described as “dirty, raunchy, deep and hard‑pushing,” giving songs like Hard To Handle and Black Peter a violent yet satisfying edge. Tom Constanten provides thick, swirling organ textures throughout, especially under the soaring jam of Mason's Children. The band builds momentum early with Easy Wind and High Time before launching into a monster 15‑minute Dancin' In The Street that showcases Bill’s steady drive and Mickey’s more subdued drumming as the era shifts. Highlights also include the crisp rendition of Saint Stephen and the heartfelt delivery of Mama Tried. Banter between songs captures the New Year’s Eve excitement, making this recording a vivid snapshot of the Dead in late‑’69 form.",
